---
title: Baked ziti
servings: 8
yield: 8 to 10 servings
tags: [italian, pork, make-ahead]
cuisine: italian
time: 1 hour 30 minutes
source: Baked Ziti by Jennifer Segal, Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/baked-ziti.html
---

Boil the @dried pasta{1%lb}(ziti) in a #large pot{} of salted water
~{7%minutes}, until very al dente. Drain and return it to the pot.

Heat the oven to 425°F (220°C) with a rack in the middle.

In a #large sauté pan{} over medium-high heat, cook the
@Italian sausage{1.5%lb}(spicy or sweet, casings removed), breaking it up,
~{5%minutes} to ~{6%minutes} until lightly browned and cooked through. Lift it
onto a plate with a #slotted spoon{}.

Pour off all but 1 tbsp of the fat, adding @olive oil{1%tbsp} if there is not
enough, and turn the heat to low. Cook the @garlic{4%cloves}(minced)
~{1%minute}, until soft but not brown.

Add the @crushed tomatoes{28%oz}, @salt{1%tsp}, @sugar{1.5%tsp} and
@red pepper flakes{1/4%tsp}. Simmer uncovered ~{10%minutes}.

Stir in the @heavy cream{1%cup}, 1/3 cup of the
@Pecorino Romano{1/3%cup}(plus 3 tbsp, grated), the sausage and the
@basil{1/3%cup}(chopped, plus more to serve). Pour it over the pasta and mix.

Spread half into a 9 x 13-inch #baking dish{}. Scatter over half the
@mozzarella{8%oz}(whole milk, shredded) and half the remaining Pecorino. Add the
rest of the pasta, then the rest of the cheeses.

Bake uncovered ~{15%minutes} to ~{20%minutes}, until melted and browned. Scatter
with basil and serve.

> To make ahead, cover and chill up to 2 days, or freeze unbaked up to 3 months
> and thaw overnight. Bake covered in foil ~{25%minutes}, then uncovered
> ~{10%minutes} to ~{15%minutes} more.
